#X text 24 55 dddd is a Lua module rather than a Pd object. Domain libraries use it to send data types that normally are not supported by Pd \, this includes: dict \, array of arrays \, and others., f 118;
#X text 24 95 This allows to create abstractions that are normally hard to be created using just Pd and the C API., f 118;
